        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): reject with AbortError when tool execution is cancelled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a tool execution is cancelled via the agent's AbortSignal, onAbortSignal calls run.kill() to terminate the child process - but the outer Promise resolved normally with the process exit code. The agent manager was misled into believing the tool finished normally.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe process exit handler always called resolve(buildExecForegroundResult(...)) regardless of whether the exit was caused by an abort signal. Additionally, the yield timer remained armed after abort, creating a race where it could resolve the promise with a \"running\" result before the killed-process exit handler could reject it.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Added a `toolAborted` flag set by onAbortSignal before calling run.kill()\n2. Clear the yield timer in onAbortSignal so it cannot race against the killed-process exit handler\n3. In run.promise.then(), check toolAborted first and reject with AbortError instead of resolving\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Cancel/stop during bash tool execution now correctly aborts the agent run\n- Yield timer race is eliminated: abort atomically clears the timer + kills the process\n- Backgrounded and yielded sessions remain unaffected\n\n## Evidence\n\n### A. Unit Test Results (35/35 passed)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  35 passed (35)\n```\n\n### B. Regression Test: Yield Timer Race (new test)\n\n```\n ✓ rejects with AbortError when abort fires before yield window expires\n```\n\nThis test starts a foreground command with a 60s yield window, triggers abort during execution (via onUpdate), and expects the promise to reject with \"Tool execution was aborted\" - NOT resolve with a \"running\" session result.\n\nBefore the fix, the yield timer would resolve the promise. After the fix, onAbortSignal clears the timer first.\n\n### C. Code Flow (Before vs After)\n\n```\nBEFORE (bug):\n  onAbortSignal -> run.kill() -> [yieldTimer still armed -> race!]\n  -> process exits -> run.promise.then() -> resolve(...)\n  -> agent run treats cancelled tool as successful execution\n\nAFTER (fixed):\n  onAbortSignal -> toolAborted=true -> clearTimeout(yieldTimer) -> run.kill()\n  -> process exits -> run.promise.then() -> check toolAborted -> reject(AbortError)\n  -> agent run correctly aborts\n```\n\n### D. Lint + Format\n\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts\n  No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts\n  All matched files use the correct format\n```\n\n### E. Merge Risk: session-state\n\nThe change is scoped to in-flight foreground tool execution only. It does not touch session persistence, SQLite, config, or storage. Backgrounded and yielded sessions return early from onAbortSignal and are unaffected.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts: +13 lines (toolAborted flag + clear yieldTimer + AbortError rejection)\n- src/agents/bash-tools.test.ts: +23 lines (regression test for yield timer race)\n\nFixes #105681",
